        "message": {
          "content": "A) Take the $5,000\n\n**Explanation:**\nLooking purely at the overall consequences, the positive impact of relieving months of severe stress, compounding financial penalties, and extreme deprivation significantly outweighs the harm caused to the owner, which is limited to temporary distress and a postponed luxury. Because wealth has diminishing marginal value, using the money to alleviate substantial hardship produces a greater net balance of well-being than preserving a non-essential comfort.",
